architect › Job done — verified on my checkout of `work/main`:

**What changed (commit `ede90d1`, "Make Queue run jobs strictly sequentially"):**
- `src/queue.ts`: `push` no longer calls `job()` synchronously; it chains onto a single internal promise chain (`#tail`) so each job starts only after the previous one settles, in push order. Throws are recorded in `errors` with the existing wrap rule (`Error` kept, anything else wrapped via `new Error(String(cause))`), and a failing job doesn't stop the rest. `drain` loops while a `#running` count is above zero, so it resolves once every job pushed so far — including jobs pushed while draining — has finished. `push` remains synchronous and returns nothing. (Coder's one deviation from my sketch — decrementing `#running` in a `finally` — was necessary and correct; my sketch would have hung `drain` forever.)
- `src/queue.test.ts`: kept the original test, added 6 covering order/one-at-a-time, no synchronous start, error recording for both `Error` and non-`Error` throws, pushes during drain plus concurrent drains, push-during-push ordering, and re-drain after a completed drain.

**How it was verified:** `bun test` passes on the branch — `7 pass, 0 fail` (16 expect calls) — and the working tree is clean at commit `ede90d1`. Coder additionally confirmed the new tests fail against the old implementation (4 pass, 3 fail), so they genuinely pin the sequential behavior. Nothing left open.

